---
import Tile from "../components/Tile.astro";
---

<div class="container">
  <h2 id="features">Why Regulus</h2>
  <div class="tiles">
    <Tile icon="/img/icon-seamless.svg" title="Seamless windows">
      Every app gets its own RemoteApp connection, so it shows up as a real window with its own icon and title. There's no wrapping desktop behind it.
    </Tile>
    <Tile icon="/img/icon-sandbox.svg" title="One Flatpak">
      QEMU, FreeRDP, and the agent all live inside the Flatpak sandbox. Close Regulus and Windows shuts down with it, so nothing keeps running in the background.
    </Tile>
    <Tile icon="/img/icon-wayland.svg" title="Wayland-native">
      Windows are drawn straight to Wayland by <code>sdl-freerdp</code>. No XWayland, no flicker, and nothing relaunches itself.
    </Tile>
    <Tile icon="/img/icon-ltsc.svg" title="Light and long-lived">
      Regulus installs Windows 11 or Windows 10 <strong>IoT Enterprise LTSC</strong>. It's a small, stable build that Microsoft supports for a decade.
    </Tile>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .tiles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
